            <ArticleTitle>RELATIONSHIP BETWEEN THE BLOOD LEVELS OF CHOLESTEROL, MUCOPROTEINS, AND FIBRINOGEN IN ISCHAEMIC HEART DISEASE.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>175-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Serum cholesterol, serum mucoproteins, and plasma fibrinogen levels were estimated in 60 male patients with ischaemic heart disease. No correlation was found between the levels of these blood components.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
